      "> Divide by 2: y < **15**",
      ">",
      "> Verify with y = 12: ⅔(12) − 5 = 8 − 5 = 3, and 3 < 5 ✓",
      ">",
      "> Verify with y = 18: ⅔(18) − 5 = 12 − 5 = 7, and 7 < 5 is false ✓",
      "",
      "> **Worked example 3 — fractions on both sides**",
      ">",
      "> Solve ½x + 2 ≥ −⅔.",
      ">",
      "> The denominators are 2 and 3, so the LCM is 6. Multiply every term by 6:",
      ">",
      "> 6 × ½x + 6 × 2 ≥ 6 × (−⅔)",
